[connection master]
[connection slave]
CALL mtr.add_suppression("Relay log write failure: could not queue event from master");
CALL mtr.add_suppression("Received oversized rotate event");
SET GLOBAL binlog_checksum= CRC32;
RESET SLAVE ALL;
include/rpl_change_topology.inc [new topology=1->2]
Warnings:
Note	####	Sending passwords in plain text without SSL/TLS is extremely insecure.
Note	####	Storing MySQL user name or password information in the master info repository is not secure and is therefore not recommended. Please consider using the USER and PASSWORD connection options for START SLAVE; see the 'START SLAVE Syntax' in the MySQL Manual for more information.
[connection master]
# Adding debug point 'binlog_sender_large_rotate_event' to @@GLOBAL.debug

# Case 1: master NONE, slave CRC32. Add checksum into rot_buf.

SET GLOBAL binlog_checksum= NONE;
[connection slave]
START SLAVE IO_THREAD;
include/wait_for_slave_io_error.inc [errno=1595 # ER_SLAVE_RELAY_LOG_WRITE_FAILURE]
Warnings:
